Imagine production:

Backend Container
Something breaks.

Bad approach:

Enter container
 ↓
Manually modify files
 ↓
Restart

Now nobody knows exactly what changed.

Better:
Fix Dockerfile/code
      ↓
Build new image
      ↓
Deploy new container
      ↓
Remove old container

This gives reproducibility.

26. Container + Image Relationship

Suppose:

resolvehub-backend:1.0

is your image.

You can run:
Container A
Container B
Container C
from that same image.

           resolvehub-backend:1.0
                      │
          ┌───────────┼───────────┐
          ↓           ↓           ↓
       Backend-1   Backend-2   Backend-3
       
This is one of the foundations for scaling applications.